---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro";
import TrustBadge from "../components/TrustBadge.astro";

const title = "Blacktop Driveway Sealer: Best Products & How to Apply (2026)";
const description = "The definitive guide to blacktop driveway sealer — what it is, the best products to buy, and how to apply it correctly to protect and restore your asphalt driveway.";

const schema = {
    "@context": "https://schema.org",
    "@type": "BlogPosting",
    headline: title,
    description: description,
    author: {
        "@type": "Person",
        name: "Alex Rivers",
    },
    datePublished: "2026-04-05",
    publisher: {
        "@type": "Organization",
        name: "The Honest Reviewers",
    },
};
---

<Layout
    title={`${title} | The Honest Reviewers`}
    description={description}
    ogType="article"
    jsonLd={schema}
    stickyCta={{
        text: "See Best Blacktop Sealers",
        link: "#best-products",
    }}
>
    <article class="relative overflow-hidden">
        <!-- Hero Section -->
        <div class="bg-gray-900 py-16 lg:py-24 relative overflow-hidden">
            <div
                class="absolute inset-0 opacity-10"
                style="background-image: url('data:image/svg+xml,%3Csvg width=\'60\' height=\'60\' viewBox=\'0 0 60 60\' xmlns=\'http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\'%3E%3Cg fill=\'none\' fill-rule=\'evenodd\'%3E%3Cg fill=\'%23ffffff\' fill-opacity=\'1\'%3E%3Cpath d=\'M36 34v-4h-2v4h-4v2h4v4h2v-4h4v-2h-4zm0-30V0h-2v4h-4v2h4v4h2V6h4V4h-4zM6 34v-4H4v4H0v2h4v4h2v-4h4v-2H6zM6 4V0H4v4H0v2h4v4h2V6h4V4H6z\'/%3E%3C/g%3E%3C/g%3E%3C/svg%3E');"
            >
            </div>
            <div class="max-w-4xl mx-auto px-4 relative z-10 text-center">
                <div class="flex justify-center mb-6">
                    <TrustBadge />
                </div>
                <h1 class="text-4xl lg:text-6xl font-black text-white leading-tight mb-8">
                    <span class="text-[#38BDF8]">Blacktop Driveway Sealer</span>: Best Products & Application Guide
                </h1>
                <p class="text-xl text-gray-300 leading-relaxed mb-8 max-w-3xl mx-auto">
                    Your blacktop driveway turns gray, brittle, and cracked without regular sealing. The right sealer restores the rich black color, blocks water infiltration, and protects against gasoline, oil, and freeze-thaw destruction. Here is what actually works.
                </p>
                <div class="flex flex-col sm:flex-row gap-4 justify-center">
                    <a
                        href="#best-products"
                        class="px-8 py-4 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-xl shadow-lg transition-all no-underline"
                    >
                        See Best Products
                    </a>
                    <a
                        href="#how-to-apply"
                        class="px-8 py-4 bg-white/10 hover:bg-white/20 text-white font-bold rounded-xl border border-white/10 no-underline"
                    >
                        How to Apply
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>

        <!-- Content -->
        <div class="max-w-3xl mx-auto px-4 py-16 lg:py-24">
            <div class="prose prose-lg prose-blue max-w-none text-gray-700 leading-relaxed">

                <p class="text-2xl font-medium text-gray-900 mb-8 italic border-l-4 border-[#38BDF8] pl-6 bg-gray-50 py-4 rounded-r-xl">
                    "Blacktop" and "asphalt" are two names for the same thing — a petroleum-based aggregate pavement. A blacktop driveway sealer is simply the common homeowner term for what the industry calls asphalt sealer or asphalt emulsion sealer. Understanding this distinction saves you from product confusion at the hardware store.
                </p>

                <p>
                    The blacktop sealer category at any hardware store is crowded and confusing. You will find products ranging from $15 per bucket to $80+, all claiming to do essentially the same thing. The truth is the formulations differ enormously — and the right choice depends on your driveway's age, condition, climate, and how long you want the results to last.
                </p>

                <p>
                    For a full breakdown of the different types of asphalt sealer available, see our complete <a href="/asphalt-sealer-for-driveways" class="text-[#1E90FF] hover:underline">asphalt sealer for driveways guide</a>. This page focuses on the specific products and application process for blacktop driveways.
                </p>

                <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6 font-sans border-b pb-4">
                    What Blacktop Driveway Sealer Actually Does
                </h2>

                <p>
                    A blacktop driveway sealer creates a protective coating over your asphalt pavement that performs four distinct functions:
                </p>

                <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 my-8">
                    <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 bg-white">
                        <div class="text-2xl mb-3">☀️</div>
                        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Blocks UV Oxidation</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm m-0">UV radiation breaks down the asphalt binder, causing the surface to fade from black to gray and become brittle. Sealer creates a sacrificial layer that absorbs UV instead of letting it reach the asphalt.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 bg-white">
                        <div class="text-2xl mb-3">💧</div>
                        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Repels Water</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm m-0">Water infiltrating surface cracks freezes, expands by 9%, and physically shatters the asphalt from within during winter. Sealer keeps water on top of the surface, not inside it.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 bg-white">
                        <div class="text-2xl mb-3">⛽</div>
                        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Resists Chemical Attack</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm m-0">Gasoline, motor oil, and antifreeze are petroleum solvents that dissolve asphalt. A quality sealer blocks these chemicals from reaching the vulnerable pavement surface.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-xl p-5 bg-white">
                        <div class="text-2xl mb-3">🎨</div>
                        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-gray-900 mb-2">Restores Appearance</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 text-sm m-0">A fresh coat of blacktop sealer restores the deep, rich black color that makes a driveway look brand new and dramatically boosts curb appeal.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h2 id="best-products" class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6 font-sans border-b pb-4">
                    Best Blacktop Driveway Sealers of 2026
                </h2>
                <p>
                    Before buying a product, see our full guide to the <a href="/best-asphalt-driveway-sealer-reviews" class="text-[#1E90FF] hover:underline">best asphalt driveway sealers</a> for complete head-to-head reviews. Here are the top performers:
                </p>

                <div class="space-y-8">
                    <div class="border-2 border-[#38BDF8] rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-md bg-white relative">
                        <div class="absolute -top-3 left-6 bg-[#FF4500] text-white font-black text-xs uppercase tracking-widest px-3 py-1 rounded-full">★ #1 Overall Pick</div>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-2 mb-2">Jetcoat 10-Year Premium Driveway Sealer</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
                            The most durable blacktop sealer available to residential homeowners. Jetcoat's coal tar polymer blend creates a thick, chemical-resistant coating that the manufacturer rates for up to 10 years of protection. The standout convenience feature is the no-stir formula — the gel consistency prevents aggregate settling, so you open the bucket and start applying immediately.
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
                            The built-in silica sand aggregate provides excellent anti-skid traction on wet blacktop and helps the sealer mechanically adhere to the surface. Coverage: approximately 250–300 sq ft per 5-gallon bucket at standard application thickness.
                        </p>
                        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-xl">
                            <ul class="m-0 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700">
                                <li><strong>Pros:</strong> Market-leading 10-year warranty, no mixing required, superior chemical resistance, jet-black color restoration, built-in traction aggregate.</li>
                                <li><strong>Cons:</strong> Coal tar formula banned in some regions (D.C., Minnesota, parts of WA/NY/WI/TX). Check local regulations first.</li>
                                <li><strong>Coverage:</strong> ~250–300 sq ft per 5-gallon bucket</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow bg-white">
                        <div class="inline-block bg-green-100 text-green-800 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3">Best Emulsion Alternative</div>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-0 mb-2">Black Jack Drive-Maxx 1000</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
                            The fastest-drying blacktop sealer in this roundup. Where most emulsion sealers require 24+ hours before foot traffic, the Drive-Maxx 1000's rapid-cure technology allows foot traffic in as little as 1 hour in warm conditions. This is transformative for households that can't keep their driveway closed all day.
                        </p>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
                            The thick consistency ensures good crack-bridging performance, and the sand-infused formula restores grip to polished, worn-out blacktop surfaces. Strong choice for driveways in mild climates where the fastest possible return to service matters most.
                        </p>
                        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-xl">
                            <ul class="m-0 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700">
                                <li><strong>Pros:</strong> Foot traffic in 1 hour, excellent thickness, sand-infused traction, widely available at major retailers.</li>
                                <li><strong>Cons:</strong> Fast drying reduces working time for corrections; avoid applying in full sun above 85°F.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow bg-white">
                        <div class="inline-block bg-blue-100 text-blue-800 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3">Best Budget Value</div>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-0 mb-2">Latex-ite Airport Grade Driveway Filler & Sealer</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
                            Originally formulated for airport runway maintenance, this budget-friendly emulsion sealer covers up to 400 sq ft per 5-gallon bucket on smooth non-porous surfaces — making it the most economical option for large driveways. The sand aggregate fills minor surface cracks while providing improved traction and adhesion.
                        </p>
                        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-xl">
                            <ul class="m-0 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700">
                                <li><strong>Pros:</strong> Best cost-per-square-foot, excellent coverage, crack-filling sand aggregate, proven long-track commercial formula.</li>
                                <li><strong>Cons:</strong> Requires very thorough mixing — heavy aggregate sinks to the bottom during shipping. Use a heavy-duty paddle mixer.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>

                    <div class="border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-8 shadow-sm hover:shadow-lg transition-shadow bg-white">
                        <div class="inline-block bg-purple-100 text-purple-800 text-xs font-bold uppercase tracking-wide px-3 py-1 rounded-full mb-3">Best Premium Option</div>
                        <h3 class="text-xl font-bold mt-0 mb-2">Pavemade Asphalt Emulsion Sealer</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-600 mb-4">
                            Contractor-grade emulsion in consumer packaging. This high-solid, latex-reinforced formula delivers the same performance used on municipal roads and commercial parking lots. It cures into a thick, hard protective layer with exceptional resistance to heavy rain, freeze-thaw cycles, and sustained vehicle traffic.
                        </p>
                        <div class="bg-gray-50 p-4 rounded-xl">
                            <ul class="m-0 space-y-2 text-sm text-gray-700">
                                <li><strong>Pros:</strong> True contractor-grade performance, extremely durable, excellent heavy-traffic resistance, professional finish quality.</li>
                                <li><strong>Cons:</strong> Higher price point than standard consumer products.</li>
                            </ul>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <!-- Quick Comparison -->
                <div class="my-16 bg-gradient-to-br from-gray-950 to-gray-900 rounded-3xl p-8 lg:p-12 text-white shadow-2xl">
                    <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-white mt-0 mb-8 border-none text-center">
                        Side-by-Side Comparison
                    </h2>
                    <div class="overflow-x-auto">
                        <table class="w-full text-sm text-left border-collapse">
                            <thead>
                                <tr class="border-b border-gray-700">
                                    <th class="py-3 px-3 text-[#38BDF8] font-bold">Product</th>
                                    <th class="py-3 px-3 text-[#38BDF8] font-bold">Lifespan</th>
                                    <th class="py-3 px-3 text-[#38BDF8] font-bold">Dry to Traffic</th>
                                    <th class="py-3 px-3 text-[#38BDF8] font-bold">Coverage / 5 gal</th>
                                </tr>
                            </thead>
                            <tbody class="text-gray-300">
                                <tr class="border-b border-gray-800">
                                    <td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-white">Jetcoat 10-Year</td>
                                    <td class="py-3 px-3">Up to 10 years</td>
                                    <td class="py-3 px-3">48–72 hours</td>
                                    <td class="py-3 px-3">~250–300 sq ft</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr class="border-b border-gray-800">
                                    <td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-white">Black Jack Drive-Maxx 1000</td>
                                    <td class="py-3 px-3">Up to 4 years</td>
                                    <td class="py-3 px-3">1–2 hours (foot)</td>
                                    <td class="py-3 px-3">~300 sq ft</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr class="border-b border-gray-800">
                                    <td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-white">Latex-ite Airport Grade</td>
                                    <td class="py-3 px-3">Up to 4 years</td>
                                    <td class="py-3 px-3">24–48 hours</td>
                                    <td class="py-3 px-3">Up to 400 sq ft</td>
                                </tr>
                                <tr>
                                    <td class="py-3 px-3 font-semibold text-white">Pavemade Emulsion</td>
                                    <td class="py-3 px-3">5+ years</td>
                                    <td class="py-3 px-3">24–48 hours</td>
                                    <td class="py-3 px-3">~250 sq ft</td>
                                </tr>
                            </tbody>
                        </table>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h2 id="how-to-apply" class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6 font-sans border-b pb-4">
                    How to Seal a Blacktop Driveway: Step-by-Step
                </h2>
                <p>
                    For a full detailed walkthrough, see our dedicated <a href="/how-to-seal-a-driveway" class="text-[#1E90FF] hover:underline">how to seal a driveway guide</a>. Here is the professional condensed version for blacktop:
                </p>

                <div class="space-y-6 my-8">
                    <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
                        <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 bg-[#FF4500] text-white font-black rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-lg">1</div>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1 mt-0">Clean the blacktop thoroughly</h3>
                            <p class="text-gray-600 m-0">Sweep, then treat all oil stains with a blacktop degreaser and stiff brush. Power-wash at 1,500–2,000 PSI. Allow 24–48 hours to dry.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
                        <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 bg-[#FF4500] text-white font-black rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-lg">2</div>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1 mt-0">Fill all cracks wider than ⅛ inch</h3>
                            <p class="text-gray-600 m-0">Sealer cannot bridge large cracks — they must be filled first with a dedicated crack filler. Cure fully before sealing. See our <a href="/best-driveway-crack-filler" class="text-[#1E90FF] hover:underline">best driveway crack fillers</a> for product recommendations.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
                        <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 bg-[#FF4500] text-white font-black rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-lg">3</div>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1 mt-0">Mask the edges</h3>
                            <p class="text-gray-600 m-0">Tape plastic sheeting or cardboard against garage doors, foundations, and adjacent concrete. Blacktop sealer permanently stains concrete and masonry.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
                        <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 bg-[#FF4500] text-white font-black rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-lg">4</div>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1 mt-0">Apply two thin coats</h3>
                            <p class="text-gray-600 m-0">Pour a ribbon across the top, pull downward with a squeegee in thin passes, then back-brush to eliminate lap marks. Wait 4–8 hours and apply a second coat perpendicular to the first. Two thin coats outperform one thick coat in every test.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                    <div class="flex gap-4 items-start">
                        <div class="flex-shrink-0 w-10 h-10 bg-[#FF4500] text-white font-black rounded-full flex items-center justify-center text-lg">5</div>
                        <div>
                            <h3 class="text-lg font-bold text-gray-900 mb-1 mt-0">Enforce the cure period</h3>
                            <p class="text-gray-600 m-0">No foot traffic for 24 hours. No vehicles for 48–72 hours. In temperatures below 65°F, wait the full 72 hours. Not sure when it's ready? Our guide on <a href="/how-long-for-driveway-sealer-to-dry" class="text-[#1E90FF] hover:underline">how long driveway sealer takes to dry</a> has the full breakdown.</p>
                        </div>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6 font-sans border-b pb-4">
                    Common Blacktop Sealing Mistakes to Avoid
                </h2>

                <div class="space-y-4 my-8">
                    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-xl p-5">
                        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-red-900 mb-1 mt-0">Sealing a new driveway too soon</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">New blacktop releases volatile oils for 6–12 months after paving. Sealing before this curing period traps the oils and creates a permanently tacky, soft surface. Wait at least 1 full year.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-xl p-5">
                        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-red-900 mb-1 mt-0">Applying over oil stains without cleaning</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Oil acts as a release agent — sealer applied over untreated oil stains will peel off in sheets within weeks. Always clean and prime oil spots first.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-xl p-5">
                        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-red-900 mb-1 mt-0">Re-sealing too frequently</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Sealing every single year builds up excessive coating thickness that buckles and peels catastrophically. Never re-seal more frequently than every 2 years, and only do so when the water bead test shows the previous coat has worn out.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div class="bg-red-50 border border-red-200 rounded-xl p-5">
                        <h3 class="text-base font-bold text-red-900 mb-1 mt-0">Applying in the wrong weather</h3>
                        <p class="text-gray-700 text-sm m-0">Below 50°F, sealers won't cure properly and may freeze in place. In full sun above 90°F, they flash-dry before penetrating the surface. The ideal window is 60–80°F with no rain forecast for 24 hours.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <h2 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mt-16 mb-6 font-sans border-b pb-4">
                    Frequently Asked Questions
                </h2>

                <div class="space-y-6">
                    <div>
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">Is blacktop sealer the same as asphalt sealer?</h4>
                        <p class="text-gray-700">Yes — completely. "Blacktop" is the common residential term for asphalt pavement. "Blacktop sealer" and "asphalt sealer" are the same category of product. Manufacturers use both terms on their packaging, which causes unnecessary confusion. When you see "blacktop driveway sealer" at the hardware store, it is interchangeable with "asphalt driveway sealer." Do not apply either type to concrete — that is a separate product category entirely.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">How much blacktop sealer do I need?</h4>
                        <p class="text-gray-700">A standard two-car driveway is approximately 400–600 square feet. Most blacktop sealers cover 250–400 sq ft per 5-gallon bucket at standard thickness, and you should plan for two coats. For a 500 sq ft driveway applying two thin coats, budget for 4 to 5 buckets. Measure your driveway (length × width) before buying and cross-reference with the specific product's stated coverage rate.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">Should I use a squeegee or brush to apply blacktop sealer?</h4>
                        <p class="text-gray-700">The professional method uses both. Pull the sealer down the driveway in thin ribbons with a rubber squeegee to force material into the surface pores and ensure even spreading. Immediately follow with a stiff-bristle brush to eliminate squeegee lap marks and pull excess material from low spots. The squeegee does the work; the brush does the finishing.</p>
                    </div>
                    <div>
                        <h4 class="font-bold text-xl text-gray-900 mb-2">Can I drive on my blacktop driveway the same day I seal it?</h4>
                        <p class="text-gray-700">No. Most blacktop sealers require a minimum of 48 hours before vehicle traffic and 72 hours in cooler weather. Driving on a freshly sealed surface leaves tire marks, pulls the coating off, and can result in sealer tracking inside the garage or onto the street. The 48–72 hour wait is non-negotiable for a professional-quality result.</p>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="mt-16 border-t border-gray-100 pt-12">
                    <h3 class="text-2xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">Related Driveway Guides</h3>
                    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-3 gap-4">
                        <a href="/best-driveway-sealer" class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition-shadow no-underline group">
                            <p class="text-[#FF4500] font-black text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">All Surfaces</p>
                            <h4 class="text-gray-900 font-bold text-lg group-hover:text-[#1E90FF] transition-colors">Best Driveway Sealers</h4>
                            <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mt-2">Our complete guide covering concrete, asphalt, and paver sealers.</p>
                        </a>
                        <a href="/asphalt-sealer-for-driveways" class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition-shadow no-underline group">
                            <p class="text-[#1E90FF] font-black text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Buyer's Guide</p>
                            <h4 class="text-gray-900 font-bold text-lg group-hover:text-[#1E90FF] transition-colors">Asphalt Sealer for Driveways</h4>
                            <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mt-2">Complete breakdown of every asphalt sealer type and when to use each one.</p>
                        </a>
                        <a href="/coal-tar-vs-asphalt-emulsion-sealer" class="bg-gray-50 border border-gray-200 rounded-2xl p-5 hover:shadow-md transition-shadow no-underline group">
                            <p class="text-green-600 font-black text-xs uppercase tracking-widest mb-2">Comparison</p>
                            <h4 class="text-gray-900 font-bold text-lg group-hover:text-[#1E90FF] transition-colors">Coal Tar vs. Asphalt Emulsion</h4>
                            <p class="text-gray-500 text-sm mt-2">Which blacktop sealer formula actually performs better?</p>
                        </a>
                    </div>
                </div>

                <div class="mt-16 text-center bg-blue-50 p-12 rounded-3xl border border-blue-100 shadow-inner">
                    <h3 class="text-3xl font-black text-gray-900 mb-6">
                        Stop the Blacktop Decline Before It Starts
                    </h3>
                    <p class="text-lg text-gray-600 mb-8 max-w-xl mx-auto">
                        Every year without sealing is a year of compounding UV damage, freeze-thaw cracking, and chemical erosion. A single weekend of DIY sealing work restores your driveway's appearance and adds years to its lifespan.
                    </p>
                    <a
                        href="#best-products"
                        class="inline-block px-10 py-5 bg-[#FF4500] hover:bg-[#E63E00] text-white font-black rounded-2xl shadow-xl shadow-[#FF4500]/30 transition-all transform hover:-translate-y-1 active:scale-95 no-underline text-xl"
                    >
                        See Our Top Product Picks
                    </a>
                </div>
            </div>
        </div>
    </article>
</Layout>
